# ── Generated chat-output strays (repository-integrity guard) ────────────────
# Something outside git writes assistant chat text into the repo as files.
# Two occurred on 2026-08-24; one was wrongly committed (see b7e5118c and
# .claude/sessions/2026-08-24.md). This guard is DELIBERATELY NARROW: it
# matches only filename shapes that no legitimate document uses — verified
# 0 hits against every tracked file under docs/. It does NOT match
# extensionless files, because legitimate ones exist (e.g. docs/implementation/PKS_ADR).
#
# THIS DOES NOT FIX THE CAUSE. The writer should be corrected at source;
# this only stops the known class being swept into a commit by accident.
docs/**/*;*
docs/**/*\*\**
